  "id": "Compound::DB00216 - Gene::3354",
  "verbalization": "Eletriptan is implicated in the interaction with Htr1e through a complex network of molecular and physiological mechanisms. The evidence suggests that Eletriptan binds to Htr1b, which in turn participates in serotonin binding, a process that is also engaged by Htr1e. This indicates a potential functional link between Eletriptan and Htr1e, possibly through the shared involvement in serotonin-related pathways. Additionally, Eletriptan is shown to cause arteriospasm coronary, which is mediated by Ergonovine, a compound that binds to Htr1e. This provides an alternative pathway through which Eletriptan may influence Htr1e, possibly via Ergonovine. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which Eletriptan could modulate Htr1e activity, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
